# ⚠ READ THE NUMBER CORRECTLY OR A CLEAN TABLE READS AS AN ALL-CLEAR IT CANNOT
# SUPPORT. These are top-level clone EVENTS, not leaf volume: synthesized deep
# `Type__clone` fns cascade into many inner leaf calls, explicit `.clone()` mints
# no CloneId, and LIR-layer emissions have no CloneId concept at all. The RANKING
# is the actionable lever — killing a top-level clone removes its entire cascade
# — and it is NOT a measure of total clone volume. Coverage is `todo/t0546`.
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.caveat = top-level clone EVENTS ranked by dynamic count, NOT leaf volume (~3.5% of aggregate array+string clone calls are attributed); C backend only; and the count is root-path sensitive on the string axis, unquantified for this aggregate, so a cross-checkout delta is not a measurement
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.cost_secs = 2400
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.input = none
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.mirror = none
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.note = the by-reason rollup and the ranked table are printed by `python3 scripts/figures.py report`; re-seed this value in the same commit that wires the report into round close
clone.waste.attributed_site_hits.note = regenerated TWICE at 3b8a5561, bit-identical both times; the second run took 145s with a warm target/ and a cached driver, so cost_secs covers a COLD release build plus a cold driver build

# ── exact-pin × measured, DB-NATIVE — the REACH RATCHET on a guard that cannot
#    catch its own class, and the reason `todo/t0851` is re-opened rather than
#    closed. `scripts/clone_meter_check.sh --anchor-age` decides "did a round
#    close?" by matching a PROSE headline, and DONE.md's round-close entries
#    have no typed marker and no enforced shape: seven shapes across ~38 closes,
#    of which the predicate matches 3. Widening it is measured to be worse (it
#    swallows mid-round entries and re-creates a false RED whose printed remedy
#    destroys the band). So the two POPULATIONS are pinned instead: a close
#    landing in a shape the predicate cannot see moves `roundish` without moving
#    `matched`, and `tests/lints.rs::done_md_round_close_shapes_are_pinned`
#    fails. ⚠ It also fires on a mid-round round-ish entry — that is the honest
#    cost of an unenforced convention, and its remedy is a 30-second
#    adjudication and a number bump, never a band re-seed.
