# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE ROUND-CLOSE GATES (R48 Track T-a2)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE CRITERION FOR THIS TABLE, stated so the enumeration says what it selects
# on (SIX QUESTIONS #3): a constant the ROUND-CLOSE BATTERY evaluates as a
# pass/fail gate on CROSS-LANE CONFORMANCE OR PARITY. Seven constants qualify.
#
# ⚠ TWO SAME-SHAPED CONSTANTS ARE DELIBERATELY OUT, named so the omission is
# visible rather than silent:
#   * tests/integration.rs:SELF_HOST_COMPREHENSION_CELL_FLOOR — a coverage pin on
#     one fixture family, not a cross-lane gate.
#   * tests/integration.rs:EXPECTED_ENTRY_POINTS — an arm-count pin. Proposed for
#     a later round in todo/t0965; adopting it here would have made this table an
#     open set, which is the failure two earlier drafts shipped.
#
# ⛔ ADOPTION IS MIRROR-MODE AND NOTHING HERE RE-PINS ANYTHING. Every value below
# was read off the constant at dc0b0024b; a value this track believed wrong would
# be a finding, never an edit.
#
# ⚠ SCAN REACH. Five of the seven take `scan = none` and say why in `caveat`:
# they are three-digit values, and tests/spec_conformance.rs — which holds four
# of them — is NOT a declared scan root, while its own re-seed log spells 237
# eleven times. A `scan = standard` there would be a waiver farm, which is how a
# guard dies (`fmt.max_width` sets the precedent).

# ── grow-only × measured — the three spec-conformance lane floors ───────────
# ⚠ THE EXTRACTOR IS LANE-ANCHORED, AND IT HAD TO BE. All three lanes print
# through the same `run_lane` formatter into one run's stderr, so a bare
# `MATCH=(?P<value>[0-9]+)` captures whichever comes first — and that is not even
# the first lane's total: a MISMATCH DETAIL containing `MATCH=` hijacks it.
# Measured against the real format strings, the bare pattern returns 9 where the
# anchored one returns 237. Anchor on the lane banner AND on `total=…`, never on
# a bare `MATCH=`.
