# ── the self-host runtime-parity trio — ONE run, three rows ────────────────
# ⭐ ALL THREE SHARE ONE REGEN STRING AND ONE regen_env, so figures.py's
# (command, env) memo spends ONE self-host corpus run on the three of them
# instead of three. The awk tail passes the whole diagnostic through unchanged
# and APPENDS one computed line: the non-MATCH count is the only one of the
# three the test does not print, and it is derivable exactly — the gate computes
# `non_excluded - matched`, and the PARITY line prints both as `matched/
# non_excluded`.
# ⚠ THE PROFILE IS PART OF THE MEASUREMENT. All three asserts no-op under
# `cfg!(debug_assertions)`, so a debug run captures numbers no gate evaluated;
# `--release` is in the command and the debug notices are in regen_forbids.
