# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE SANITIZE GATES (R48 Track T-a2)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE CRITERION FOR THIS TABLE: a constant pinned by the sanitize allowlist lint
# or by the sweep itself — a number stating how much sanitizer debt is tolerated,
# or how much of the corpus is covered. Twelve rows.
#
# ⚠ ENUMERATED WITH BOTH HALVES OF todo/t0926's declaration-shaped scan — a Rust
# `const` scan AND a shell one — because the Rust half is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to
# `${VAR:-N}` defaults, and the two shell rows below (COVERAGE_FLOOR,
# UNKNOWN_CEILING) live only in that half. A closed grep for five known names
# cannot show you what it omits.
# ⚠ CORRUPTION_CEILING is here for the same reason: it sits in the SAME lint
# function, is parsed by the SAME `read()` helper and carries its own
# `assert_eq!` a few lines from LEAK_CEILING's. Identical shape ⇒ its absence
# from an earlier enumeration was an accident, not a decision (Core #4).
# ⚠ The six ZERO-valued ceilings beside them in scripts/sanitize_sweep.sh
# (UBSAN / TIMEOUT / INFRA / CRASH / FLAKY / CLASS_UNSTABLE) are correctly OUT: a
# zero-valued ceiling has nothing to mirror and nothing to trend.
#
# ⭐ ALL FIVE LEAK CONSTANTS ARE `assert_eq!`, i.e. EXACT PINS, not `<=`
# ceilings — regenerated at dc0b0024b by reading each of the five consumers. The
# lint says why in its own words: under `<=` a burn-down that forgets to lower
# the number is silently accepted and the leftover headroom quietly admits the
# next leak. COVERAGE_FLOOR is the only genuine floor in the family.
#
# ── WHY ROWS 1-6 ARE PAIRS AND 7-8 ARE NOT ─────────────────────────────────
# The pair shape is owed to the three totals that measure LEAK DEBT MAGNITUDE —
# rows · records · class_pairs — and to nothing else. It exists because those
# three MOVE IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS inside one round and the lint says so in its
# own comment: R48 deleted 16 rows and admitted 3, so rows FELL while records
# ROSE. A reader watching one total scores that round as a pure burn-down; a
# reader watching another scores it as a regression; both readings are wrong
# alone. The `.round_open` half is what makes the round's NET movement readable
# at all. `loose_signatures` and `uncited_class_pairs` are anti-gaming and
# burn-down counters, not debt magnitude — and `uncited`'s TARGET IS 0, so a
# trend pair on it would be noise.
# ⚠ AND THE PAIR IS NOT THE CLONE METERS' PAIR. There, BOTH halves are code
# constants and clone_band_anchor_is_reseeded_before_work_resumes watches the
# anchor. Here only `.pin` has a constant; `.round_open` is DB-NATIVE, carries
# `mirror = none`, and NOTHING re-seeds it at round open. Its regen follows the
# tree's one declared round-open anchor (tests/integration.rs `ROUND-OPENED-BY:`)
# rather than hard-coding a sha, so it goes RED once that anchor moves and this
# value has not — but only for someone who RUNS it. See each row's caveat.

row = sanitize.leak.rows.pin
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.value = 294
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.unit = rows in tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt (one per leaking fixture)
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.polarity = exact-pin
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.provenance = derived
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.authority = tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt — the lint counts its non-comment, non-blank lines; LEAK_CEILING is a hand-kept pin of that count
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.regen = awk -F'\t' '{t=$0; sub(/^[ \t]*/,"",t); if(t ~ /^#/) next; g=$0; gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",g); if(g=="") next; rows++; ns=split($2,S,","); for(i=1;i<=ns;i++){s=S[i]; gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",s); if(s=="") continue; n=s; sub(/^.*\*/,"",n); if(n ~ /\+$/){loose++; sub(/\+$/,"",n)} pairs++; records+=n+0}} END{print "leak-allowlist census: rows=" rows+0 " pairs=" pairs+0 " records=" records+0 " loose=" loose+0 " (scanned " NR " lines)"}' tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.regen_extract = census: rows=(?P<value>[0-9]+) pairs=
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.regen_fires = \(scanned [1-9][0-9]* lines\)
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.regen_env = none
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.instrument = an awk census over the allowlist, applying the same non-comment/non-blank filter as tests/lints.rs::sanitize_allowlists_shrink_only's `read()` helper
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.measured_at = dc0b0024b
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.home = tests/lints.rs:LEAK_CEILING
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.scan = none
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.caveat = scan = none — 294 has 33 unmasked spellings across the roots (14 in tests/integration.rs, 3 in scripts/clone_meter.spec, one each in nine todo/ items) because it is also the R47 cross-checkout clone discrepancy; a waiver farm on that scale is how a guard dies. ⚠ AND A ROW COUNT IS NOT LEAK VOLUME: it counts FIXTURES, and one fixture's row can tolerate five mechanisms and dozens of records — read it with `records` and `class_pairs` or not at all
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.cost_secs = 30
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.mirror = tests/lints.rs:LEAK_CEILING
sanitize.leak.rows.pin.input = none

row = sanitize.leak.rows.round_open
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.value = 294
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.unit = rows in tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt at the declared round-open anchor
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.polarity = exact-pin
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.provenance = derived
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.authority = tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt as of the commit named by the `ROUND-OPENED-BY:` line in tests/integration.rs — the tree's ONE declared round-open anchor, read rather than copied
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.regen = git show "$(grep -m1 -oE 'ROUND-OPENED-BY: [0-9a-f]+' tests/integration.rs | cut -d' ' -f2)":tests/sanitize/LEAK_ALLOWLIST.txt | awk -F'\t' '{t=$0; sub(/^[ \t]*/,"",t); if(t ~ /^#/) next; g=$0; gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",g); if(g=="") next; rows++; ns=split($2,S,","); for(i=1;i<=ns;i++){s=S[i]; gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/,"",s); if(s=="") continue; n=s; sub(/^.*\*/,"",n); if(n ~ /\+$/){loose++; sub(/\+$/,"",n)} pairs++; records+=n+0}} END{print "leak-allowlist census: rows=" rows+0 " pairs=" pairs+0 " records=" records+0 " loose=" loose+0 " (scanned " NR " lines)"}'
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.regen_extract = census: rows=(?P<value>[0-9]+) pairs=
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.regen_fires = \(scanned [1-9][0-9]* lines\)
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.regen_env = none
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.instrument = the same awk census, fed by `git show` at the anchor the tree declares
sanitize.leak.rows.round_open.measured_at = dc0b0024b
